    "explanation": "<p class=\"text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">A number is in correct standard form if it is written as <strong>A × 10<sup>n</sup></strong> where <strong>1 ≤ A &lt; 10</strong> and <strong>n</strong> is an integer. If the decimal part <em>A</em> is not within this range, adjust by moving the decimal point and changing the power of 10 accordingly.</p>",
